CONVERSATION 1: 38, AMH 0.6, four months trying, still deciding about IVF

Lead: I'm 38 and my AMH came back at 0.6. My doctor said IVF is really my only option now. We've only been trying 4 months.

Sonia: An AMH of 0.6 is low, but on its own it doesn't tell the whole story about what's still possible for you. Your doctor may well be right that IVF is the best path here, and I wouldn't second guess that. Where I could add value is helping you optimize the biology behind that cycle, things like egg quality, inflammation and your overall health. Are you already moving toward a cycle, or still figuring out the next steps?

Lead: Still figuring it out. IVF feels like such a big step and I don't feel I can make that decision this quickly.

Sonia: That makes a lot of sense. Four months isn't very long, and a low AMH result can make everything feel more urgent than it actually needs to be. To be clear, I'm not a doctor and I can't tell you whether or when IVF is the right call, that's between you and your team. What I can help with is making sure your body is in the best possible shape while you take the time you need to decide, whether that ends up being natural conception, IVF, or something in between. Can I ask, is having a baby one of your biggest priorities at the moment?

Lead: It's the main thing in our life right now. We think about it constantly.

Sonia: Then these next few months are worth using rather than spending on waiting. Are you navigating this with a partner, or are you doing this on your own?

Lead: With my husband. He's completely on board, he just doesn't know what to do either.

Sonia: That's very common, and it's much easier when you both hear the same information at the same time. Just so you know, the support I offer is a paid coaching program, personalized to your situation, and it asks for real participation rather than only an investment. Would that be something you'd be open to if it turned out to be the right fit?

Lead: Yes, if it genuinely helps.

Sonia: A consultation with my team would let us understand your full picture, your history, your labs and your cycles, and see where there's room to work before you decide anything about IVF. Here's where you can pick a time that suits you both.

